                                                "sense_id": "7d6fefb9-2963-3c10-a544-797a67968049",
                                                "text": "Railway workers were therefore a perfect subject for research, given the varied roles they undertook. If infection was greatest among the non-public-facing staff, it would suggest – given most worked outside – that contraction was caused by something found in the \"atmosphere at large\". If affliction was higher among the indoor and public-facing staff, it would suggest that human contact was the cause. And it was the latter point that was proven."
